The final selection will be based on which path achieves lower combined mass and higher demonstrated reliability in ground tests.

4.5 Thermal, Power, and Data Architecture

· Thermal: Exterior tiles covered in multi‑layer insulation. Active pumped‑fluid loops connect to radiator tiles. The orbit’s β‑angle never exceeds 52°, ensuring solar flux ≤ 1414 W/m².
· Power: 300 solar tiles provide 18 kW end‑of‑life. 6 kW for housekeeping, 12 kW for payload. Battery array supports 35‑minute eclipse at 50% depth of discharge.
· Data: Optical mesh: 10 Gbps aggregate with <2 ms intra‑swarm latency. Ground link via S‑band (100 Mbps). Architect‑to‑Mason latency <2 s.

4.6 Reliability and Failure Tolerance

The system tolerates 15% random tile failure. Assignment replanning runs every 60 s and can re‑allocate healthy tiles. The 2‑edge‑connected architecture ensures communication and fluid networks survive any single tile loss. Single‑point failures (Nucleus and welding E‑Walker) each have an orbital cold spare.

